# Complete: Audit and Auto-Improve to 100%

## Purpose

This convenience rule combines **audit** and **update** into a single operation: assess a kind's current state and automatically bring it to 100% (or target score) completion by filling all identified gaps.

## Role

You are the Planton Code Partner. This rule orchestrates a complete quality improvement workflow: audit → identify gaps → fill gaps → verify completion.

## When to Use Complete

Use complete when you want to:
- ✅ **Bring kind to 100%** - One command to achieve ideal state
- ✅ **Quick quality improvement** - No need to manually run audit then update
- ✅ **Batch improvement** - Rapidly improve multiple kinds
- ✅ **Quality gates** - Ensure kinds meet standards before release
- ✅ **Onboarding existing kinds** - Systematically complete legacy kinds

**Use manual audit/update when:**
- ❌ You only want to check status (just audit)
- ❌ You want to control which gaps to fill (manual update with specific scenario)
- ❌ You want to preview changes first (use update --dry-run)
- ❌ Kind is already complete (no work needed)

## Usage

### Basic Syntax

```
@complete-catalog-kind <KindName> [flags]
```

### Examples

**Simplest usage:**
```bash
@complete-catalog-kind CloudflareD1Database
```

**With target score:**
```bash
@complete-catalog-kind GcpCertManagerCert --target-score 90
```

**Preview mode:**
```bash
@complete-catalog-kind KubernetesPostgres --dry-run
```

## Workflow

### Step 1: Initial Audit

**Action:** Run audit to assess current state

```
🔍 Auditing CloudflareD1Database...

Current State:
  Overall Score: 65%
  Status: Partially Complete
  
Missing Items:
  ❌ Terraform module (4.44%)
  ❌ Kind guide GUIDE.md (13.34%)
  ❌ Pulumi module README (5%)
  ⚠️  Examples incomplete (3.33%)

Audit report delivered in session
```

**Decision Logic:**

```
IF score ≥ target_score (default 95%):
  → Report "Already complete!" and exit
  
IF score < target_score:
  → Proceed to Step 2 (fill gaps)
```

### Step 2: Fill Gaps (if needed)

**Action:** Run update --fill-gaps to complete kind

```
🔄 Completing CloudflareD1Database (65% → 95%+)...

Phase 1: Generate Terraform Module
[1/7] ✅ Generated variables.tf (matches spec.proto)
[2/7] ✅ Generated provider.tf
[3/7] ✅ Generated locals.tf
[4/7] ✅ Generated main.tf
[5/7] ✅ Generated outputs.tf
[6/7] ✅ Generated README.md
[7/7] ✅ Passed terraform validate

Phase 2: Generate Documentation
[8/8] ✅ Wrote GUIDE.md (kind guide)

Phase 3: Enhance Presets
[10/10] ✅ Verified presets match current spec.proto

Phase 4: Final Validation
[11/14] ✅ Proto stubs regenerated (make protos)
[12/14] ✅ Kind tests passed (go test ./catalog/<provider>/<kind>/...)
[13/14] ✅ Build validation passed (go build ./catalog/<provider>/<kind>/...)
[14/14] ✅ Kind tests passed (go test -v ./catalog/<provider>/<kind>/...)
```

**What Gets Created:**

The update --fill-gaps scenario will run appropriate forge flow rules to create:
- Missing proto files (if any)
- Missing IaC modules (Pulumi or Terraform)
- Missing documentation (guide, user-facing, presets)
- Missing supporting files (e2e manifests, module READMEs)
- Missing `GUIDE.md` (authored wisdom seeded per forge flow rule 019, following
  `_rules/docs/write-catalog-kind-guide.mdc`) -- followed by
  `make generate-reference` so the reference page's guide link and the catalog
  indexes stay fresh (the reference freshness gate fails otherwise)

**Validation (Execute in Sequence):**
- After proto file creation/changes: Run `make protos` to regenerate Go stubs
- After each creation: Validate builds and tests pass
- Run kind-specific tests: `go test ./catalog/<provider>/<kind>/...`
  - Validates buf.validate rules in spec.proto are correct
  - Validates spec_test.go tests pass with current validation logic
- After Pulumi/Go code changes: Run `go build ./catalog/<provider>/<kind>/...` to validate complete build
- Run full test suite: `go test -v ./catalog/<provider>/<kind>/...` to validate all tests pass
- Retries up to 3 times on fixable errors
- Reports progress in real-time

**Critical:** Kind tests (spec_test.go) must pass for kind to be considered complete. Failing tests indicate validation rules are incorrect or need updating.

### Step 3: Final Audit

**Action:** Re-run audit to verify completion

```
🔍 Re-auditing CloudflareD1Database...

Final State:
  Overall Score: 98%
  Status: Functionally Complete
  
Remaining Items:
  ⚠️  1 minor item (Terraform E2E test logs)

Re-audit report delivered in session
```

### Step 4: Summary Report

**Action:** Show before/after comparison

```
✅ Completion Successful: CloudflareD1Database

Before:
  Score: 65%
  Status: Partially Complete
  Missing: 4 items

After:
  Score: 98%
  Status: Functionally Complete
  Missing: 1 minor item

Improvement: +33% (65% → 98%)

Files Created:
  ✅ iac/tf/ (6 files) - Terraform module
  ✅ GUIDE.md - Kind guide (authored judgment)
  ✅ Verified presets are up to date

Audit Reports:
  📊 Before: audit delivered in session
  📊 After: re-audit delivered in session

Duration: 18 minutes

Next Steps:
  1. Review generated files
  2. Test deployment with: e2e/manifest.yaml
  3. Commit changes:
     git add -A
     git commit -m "improve: complete CloudflareD1Database to 98%"
```

## Flags and Options

### --dry-run

Preview what would be done without making changes:

```bash
@complete-catalog-kind CloudflareD1Database --dry-run
```

**Output:**
```
🔍 Dry-Run: Complete CloudflareD1Database

Current State (from audit):
  Score: 65%
  Missing:
    ❌ Terraform module (4.44%)
    ❌ Kind guide (13.34%)
    ⚠️  Examples incomplete (3.33%)

Planned Actions:
  1. Run forge rules 013-015 → Create Terraform module
  2. Run forge rule 019 → Write GUIDE.md
  3. Run validation (rules 018-019)

Expected Result:
  Score: 98% (+33%)
  Duration: ~15-20 minutes
  Files Created: ~12

No files will be modified (dry-run mode)

To proceed: remove --dry-run flag
```

### --target-score <percentage>

Stop when target score is reached:

```bash
@complete-catalog-kind CloudflareD1Database --target-score 90
```

**Behavior:**
- If current score ≥ 90%, exits immediately (already at target)
- If current score < 90%, fills gaps until ≥90%
- Doesn't necessarily reach 100% (stops at target)

**Use when:**
- You want "good enough" not "perfect"
- Time-constrained (90% might be achievable in 10 min vs 100% in 30 min)
- Some gaps are acceptable (e.g., missing examples is ok for your use case)

**Default target:** 95% (functionally complete)

### --skip-validation

Skip final build and test validation (faster but riskier):

```bash
@complete-catalog-kind CloudflareD1Database --skip-validation
```

**Warning:** Use only when confident updates won't break builds.

